Notebook[
 {Cell["Chapter 4 companion: the undifferentiated difference (section 4.2)", 
   "Title"], Cell["Thesis: Comparing UV Regularizations for Cosmological \
Correlators in de Sitter Space, Sanam Limbu (LMU Munich, 2026), Chapter 4. \
Notation: a = k12, b = k34, and k is the exchanged momentum. 14.3.0 for \
Microsoft Windows (64-bit) (July 8, 2025).", "Text"], 
  Cell["This notebook checks the computer-algebra steps of section 4.2; the \
key result is the boxed difference (4.24).\nExact checks return residual 0 \
for generic a, b, k > 0 (pairwise different).\nNumerical checks state the \
digits of relative agreement reached; a precision goal is not an error \
bound.\nEvaluate top to bottom in a fresh kernel. The ledger at the end lists \
every check.\nThe notebook does not need the derivative notebook. The ansatz \
search and the bounds behind the large-k limit are not part of it.", "Text"], 
  Cell["Setup", "Section"], Cell["ClearAll[\"Global`*\"];\n$MaxExtraPrecision \
= 10000;\n(* generic positive kinematics: a = k12, b = k34, k = exchanged \
momentum *)\nasm = a > 0 && b > 0 && k > 0 && a != b && a != k && b != \
k;\nledger = {};\nsec = \"\";\n\n(* all logarithm arguments below are \
positive: split products and quotients *)\nlogExpand[e_] := \
Together[PowerExpand[e /. Log[z_] :> Log[Factor[z]]] /. Log[4] -> 2 \
Log[2]];\n\n(* exact check: the residual must reduce to 0, otherwise the \
build stops *)\ncheckExact[name_, eq_, residual_] := Module[{r = residual},\n \
 Scan[If[r =!= 0, r = #[residual]] &,\n    {Together, Expand, Simplify[#, \
Assumptions -> asm] &,\n     FullSimplify[#, Assumptions -> asm] &}];\n  If[r \
=!= 0, Print[\"FAILED: \", name]; Print[residual]; Abort[]];\n  \
AppendTo[ledger, {sec, name, eq, \"exact\", 0, Infinity}];\n  0];\n\n(* \
numerical check: records the digits of relative agreement reached \
*)\ncheckNum[name_, eq_, got_, want_, digits_] := Module[{d, rel, n},\n  d = \
Quiet[N[got, digits + 10] - N[want, digits + 10], {N::meprec, N::precw}];\n  \
rel = Abs[d]/Max[1, Abs[N[want, 20]]];\n  n = If[rel == 0, digits + 10, \
Floor[-Log10[rel]]];\n  If[n < digits, Print[\"FAILED: \", name, \" \", n]; \
Abort[]];\n  AppendTo[ledger, {sec, name, eq, \"numerical\", ToString[n] <> \
\" digits\", n}];\n  n];\n\n(* short PASS line for the current section \
*)\npass[] := Module[{r = Select[ledger, First[#] === sec &], nd},\n  nd = \
Cases[r, {_, _, _, \"numerical\", _, n_} :> n];\n  \"PASS \" <> sec <> \": \" \
<> ToString[Count[r, {_, _, _, \"exact\", __}]] <> \" exact\"\n   <> If[nd \
=== {}, \"\", \", \" <> ToString[Length[nd]] <> \" numerical (at least \"\n   \
  <> ToString[Min[nd]] <> \" digits)\"]]", "Input"], 
  Cell["4.2.3  The closed form", "Section"], Cell["(4.24)  boxed difference, \
Delta = 2 pi^3 [P+/(a+b) + P-/(a-b)]\n(4.25)  P+\n(4.26)  P-\nTyped as \
printed. No check in this cell; the later cells use these definitions.", 
   "Text"], Cell["(* (4.25): P+ ; u = k12, v = k34, t = k *)\nPp[u_, v_, t_] \
:= (Zeta[3]\n  - PolyLog[3, (u - t)/(u + t)] - PolyLog[3, (v - t)/(v + t)]\n  \
- PolyLog[3, (u - t) (v - t)/((u + t) (v + t))]\n  - 2 (PolyLog[3, -(u - \
t)/(2 t)] + PolyLog[3, -(v - t)/(2 t)])\n  + PolyLog[3, -(u - t)/(v + t)] + \
PolyLog[3, -(v - t)/(u + t)]\n  + Log[(u + t) (v + t)/(4 t^2)] (PolyLog[2, \
-(u - t)/(2 t)] + PolyLog[2, -(v - t)/(2 t)])\n  + Log[(u + t) (v + t)/(4 \
t^2)]^3/6);\n\n(* (4.26): P- *)\nPm[u_, v_, t_] := (2 (PolyLog[3, (u - t)/(u \
+ t)] - PolyLog[3, (v - t)/(v + t)])\n  + 2 (PolyLog[3, -(u - t)/(2 t)] - \
PolyLog[3, -(v - t)/(2 t)])\n  - Log[(u + t) (v + t)/(4 t^2)] (PolyLog[2, -(u \
- t)/(2 t)] - PolyLog[2, -(v - t)/(2 t)])\n  + Pi^2/6 Log[(u + t)/(v + t)]\n  \
- (Log[(u + t)/(2 t)]^3 - Log[(v + t)/(2 t)]^3)/3);\n\n(* (4.24): the boxed \
difference *)\nDelta24[u_, v_, t_] := 2 Pi^3 (Pp[u, v, t]/(u + v) + Pm[u, v, \
t]/(u - v));", "Input"], Cell["4.2.3  Landen and the five-term relation", 
   "Section"], Cell["(4.19)  Landen, for r12 and r34 as in the first line of \
(4.20) and its image\n(4.28)  five-term relation in the form used\nExact: the \
Landen partners and logarithms; both sides of (4.28) vanish at b = k and \
their b-derivatives agree.\nNumerical: (4.19) and (4.28) at two points; the \
second has k > a, b.", "Text"], Cell["sec = \"4.2.3, Landen and \
(4.28)\";\n\n(* the arguments: r12, r34 of (4.27), and the four arguments of \
(4.21) *)\nra = (a - k)/(a + k); rb = (b - k)/(b + k);\nna = -(a - k)/(2 k); \
nb = -(b - k)/(2 k);\nca = -(a - k)/(b + k); cb = -(b - k)/(a + k);\nlA = \
Log[(a + k)/(2 k)]; lB = Log[(b + k)/(2 k)];\ncanon[e_] := e /. PolyLog[2, \
z_] :> PolyLog[2, Together[z]];\n\n(* (4.19) with w = r12 and r34, as in the \
first line of (4.20) and its image *)\nlanden[w_] := -PolyLog[2, w/(w - 1)] - \
Log[1 - w]^2/2;\ncheckExact[\"Landen partners of r12, r34\", \"(4.20)\",\n  \
Together[ra/(ra - 1) - na] + Together[rb/(rb - 1) - \
nb]];\ncheckExact[\"Landen logarithms of r12, r34\", \"(4.20)\",\n  \
Expand[logExpand[Log[1 - ra]^2 - lA^2 + Log[1 - rb]^2 - \
lB^2]]];\nDo[checkNum[\"Landen (4.19) for r12, r34 at (a,b,k) = \" <> \
ToString[pt, InputForm], \"(4.19)\",\n    Max[Map[Abs[N[PolyLog[2, #], 40] + \
N[PolyLog[2, #/(# - 1)], 40] + N[Log[1 - #]^2/2, 40]] &,\n      {ra, rb} /. \
Thread[{a, b, k} -> pt]]], 0, 25],\n  {pt, {{13/10, 17/10, 7/10}, {1/2, 4/5, \
3}}}];\n\n(* (4.28): both sides vanish at b = k and the b-derivatives agree \
(all logarithms positive,\n   all arguments below 1 for positive momenta) \
*)\nfiveL = PolyLog[2, ra rb];\nfiveR = PolyLog[2, ca] + PolyLog[2, cb] - \
PolyLog[2, na] - PolyLog[2, nb] - lA lB;\nfive = canon[fiveL - \
fiveR];\ncheckExact[\"(4.28) vanishes at b = k\", \"(4.28)\", logExpand[five \
/. b -> k]];\ncheckExact[\"(4.28) b-derivatives agree\", \"(4.28)\", \
logExpand[canon[D[five, b]]]];\nDo[checkNum[\"(4.28) at (a,b,k) = \" <> \
ToString[pt, InputForm], \"(4.28)\",\n    fiveL /. Thread[{a, b, k} -> pt], \
fiveR /. Thread[{a, b, k} -> pt], 30],\n  {pt, {{13/10, 17/10, 7/10}, {1/2, \
4/5, 3}}}];  (* second point: k > a, b *)\npass[]", "Input"], 
  Cell[BoxData["\"PASS 4.2.3, Landen and (4.28): 4 exact, 4 numerical (at \
least 35 digits)\""], "Output"], Cell["4.2.3  The derivative of (4.24)", 
   "Section"], Cell["(4.21)  boxed derivative, typed as printed\nThe \
k-derivative of (4.24), reduced with Landen and (4.28), leaves four distinct \
dilogarithms and equals 2k times (4.21).", "Text"], 
  Cell["sec = \"4.2.3, derivative\";\n\n(* (4.21) as printed *)\nres421[u_, \
v_, t_] := Pi^3/t (\n  (PolyLog[2, -(v - t)/(u + t)] - PolyLog[2, -(v - t)/(2 \
t)] + Log[(u + t)/(2 t)]^2/2)/((u - t) (v + t))\n  + (PolyLog[2, -(u - t)/(v \
+ t)] - PolyLog[2, -(u - t)/(2 t)] + Log[(v + t)/(2 t)]^2/2)/((u + t) (v - \
t))\n  + Log[(u + t)/(2 t)] Log[(v + t)/(2 t)]/((u - t) (v - t))\n  - \
(PolyLog[2, -(u - t)/(2 t)] + PolyLog[2, -(v - t)/(2 t)] + Pi^2/6)/((u + t) \
(v + t)));\n\n(* Landen replaces the dilogarithms of r12 and r34, (4.28) that \
of r12 r34 *)\nreduceLi[z_] := Which[\n  z === Together[ra], landen[ra],\n  z \
=== Together[rb], landen[rb],\n  z === Together[ra rb], fiveR,\n  True, \
PolyLog[2, z]];\n\n(* the k-derivative of (4.24), reduced *)\nreduced = \
canon[canon[D[Delta24[a, b, k], k]] /. PolyLog[2, z_] :> reduceLi[z]];\n\n(* \
four distinct dilogarithms remain, as in (4.21) *)\nfour = Sort[Together /@ \
{na, nb, ca, cb}];\nremain = Sort[DeleteDuplicates[Cases[reduced, PolyLog[2, \
z_] :> z, Infinity]]];\ncheckExact[\"four dilogarithms remain\", \"(4.21)\", \
Boole[remain =!= four]];\n\n(* the four become symbols, the logarithms are \
expanded; compare with 2 k (4.21) *)\nliOf = <|Together[na] -> liA, \
Together[nb] -> liB, Together[ca] -> liC, Together[cb] -> \
liD|>;\nsymbolize[e_] := canon[e] /. PolyLog[2, z_] :> \
liOf[z];\ncheckExact[\"d/dk of (4.24) = 2 k (4.21)\", \"(4.21), (4.24)\",\n  \
logExpand[symbolize[reduced] - symbolize[2 k res421[a, b, k]]]];\npass[]", 
   "Input"], Cell[BoxData["\"PASS 4.2.3, derivative: 2 exact\""], "Output"], 
  Cell["4.2.3  Large k", "Section"], Cell["The trilogarithm arguments tend to \
-1, -1, 1/2, 1/2, 1, 1, 1, and P+ and P- tend to 0, from the special values \
of Li3 and Li2.\nThis checks only these limits, not the bounds behind the \
large-k limit of the integral.", "Text"], Cell["sec = \"4.2.3, large \
k\";\n\n(* trilogarithm arguments as k -> Infinity: r12, r34, na, nb, r12 \
r34, ca, cb *)\nlimits = Limit[{ra, rb, na, nb, ra rb, ca, cb}, k -> \
Infinity, Assumptions -> a > 0 && b > 0];\ncheckExact[\"trilogarithm \
arguments tend to -1, 1/2, 1, 1\", \"4.2.3\",\n  Boole[limits =!= {-1, -1, \
1/2, 1/2, 1, 1, 1}]];\n\n(* k -> Infinity inside every polylogarithm and \
logarithm; Li_n is continuous at -1, 1/2, 1.\n   The zeta(3), pi^2 log 2 and \
log^3 2 terms cancel, using the closed form of Li3(1/2) *)\natInf[e_] := e /. \
{\n  PolyLog[n_, z_] :> PolyLog[n, Limit[z, k -> Infinity, Assumptions -> a > \
0 && b > 0]],\n  Log[z_] :> Log[Limit[z, k -> Infinity, Assumptions -> a > 0 \
&& b > 0]]};\ncheckExact[\"P+ tends to 0\", \"(4.25)\", \
logExpand[FunctionExpand[atInf[Pp[a, b, k]]]]];\ncheckExact[\"P- tends to \
0\", \"(4.26)\", logExpand[FunctionExpand[atInf[Pm[a, b, k]]]]];\npass[]", 
   "Input"], Cell[BoxData["\"PASS 4.2.3, large k: 3 exact\""], "Output"], 
  Cell["4.2.3  (4.24) against (4.22)", "Section"], 
  Cell["(4.22)  Delta as minus the integral of 2k' times (4.21) from k to \
infinity\nNumerical, at two points; the second has k > a, b.", "Text"], 
  Cell["sec = \"4.2.3, (4.22)\";\n\n(* (4.22): minus the integral of 2 t \
(4.21) from k to infinity, split at k12 and k34 *)\ntail[u_, v_, t0_] := \
-NIntegrate[2 t res421[u, v, t],\n  Evaluate[Join[{t, t0}, Sort[Select[{u, v, \
10}, # > t0 &]], {Infinity}]],\n  WorkingPrecision -> 20, PrecisionGoal -> \
12, MaxRecursion -> 12,\n  Method -> {\"GlobalAdaptive\", \
\"SymbolicProcessing\" -> 0}];\n\nDo[checkNum[\"(4.24) vs (4.22) at (a,b,k) = \
\" <> ToString[pt, InputForm], \"(4.22), (4.24)\",\n    Delta24 @@ pt, tail \
@@ pt, 12],\n  {pt, {{13/10, 17/10, 7/10}, {4/5, 3/2, 5/2}}}];  (* second \
point: k > a, b *)\npass[]", "Input"], 
  Cell[BoxData[
    "\"PASS 4.2.3, (4.22): 0 exact, 2 numerical (at least 19 digits)\""], 
   "Output"], Cell["4.2.1, 4.2.3  Direct integration of (3.17)", "Section"], 
  Cell["(4.23)  [PZP] with the external times first, then the loop energies, \
the middle time last\nThe loop factor is the energy integral of (4.23). Its \
closed form is compared with LevinRule quadrature for k below k12, above k12 \
and close to k12.", "Text"], Cell["sec = \"4.2.1, 4.2.3, direct \
integration\";\n\n(* loop factor of (4.23): the p integral of k12 \
log(p^2+k^2) cos(pz)/(p^2+k12^2) over the real line.\n   Log[Abs[..]] is \
needed for k > k12; u = k12, t = k *)\nloopF[u_?NumericQ, t_?NumericQ, \
z_?NumericQ] := (Pi Exp[-u z] Log[Abs[t^2 - u^2]]\n  - Pi Exp[-u z] \
ExpIntegralEi[(u - t) z] + Pi Exp[u z] ExpIntegralEi[-(u + t) \
z]);\nloopNum[u_, t_, z_] := 2 NIntegrate[u Log[p^2 + t^2] Cos[p z]/(p^2 + \
u^2), {p, 0, Infinity},\n  Method -> \"LevinRule\", WorkingPrecision -> 22, \
PrecisionGoal -> 14, MaxRecursion -> 30];\nDo[checkNum[\"loop factor vs \
LevinRule at (k12, k, z) = \" <> ToString[pt, InputForm], \"(4.23)\",\n    \
loopF @@ pt, loopNum @@ pt, 12],\n  {pt, {{13/10, 7/10, 1}, {4/5, 5/2, 6/5}, \
{1, 1000001/1000000, 1}}}];  (* k < k12, k > k12, k near k12 *)", "Input"], 
  Cell["(3.17)  the single-energy line and [PZP] of (4.23), integrated \
numerically and compared with (4.24).\nThe digits reached are the precision \
goal of these integrations; the Python script reaches about 30 digits.", 
   "Text"], Cell["(* external-time transforms of 1, log z, log^2 z: (4.3), \
(4.4) and the same for log^2 z *)\nt0[c_, p_] := c/(p^2 + c^2);\nt1[c_, p_] \
:= -Re[(EulerGamma + Log[c - I p])/(c - I p)];\nt2[c_, p_] := Re[((EulerGamma \
+ Log[c - I p])^2 + Pi^2/6)/(c - I p)];\nline[f_] := 2 NIntegrate[f[p], {p, \
0, 1, 10, Infinity},\n  WorkingPrecision -> 16, PrecisionGoal -> 10, \
MaxRecursion -> 10,\n  Method -> {\"GlobalAdaptive\", \"SymbolicProcessing\" \
-> 0}];\n\n(* (3.17): the single-energy line, times -Pi^2, and [PZP] of \
(4.23) with the middle time last, times -Pi *)\ndeltaDirect[u_, v_, t_] := \
Module[{mom, single, pzp},\n  mom[p_] := Log[p^2 + t^2];\n  single = \
line[Function[p, mom[p] (t2[u, p] t0[v, p] - 2 t1[u, p] t1[v, p] + t0[u, p] \
t2[v, p])\n    - mom[p]^2 (t1[u, p] t0[v, p] + t0[u, p] t1[v, p])]];\n  pzp = \
Block[{$MaxExtraPrecision = 20}, NIntegrate[2 Log[z] loopF[u, t, z] loopF[v, \
t, z],\n    {z, 0, 1, 10, Infinity}, WorkingPrecision -> 16, PrecisionGoal -> \
10, MaxRecursion -> 10,\n    Method -> {\"GlobalAdaptive\", \
\"SymbolicProcessing\" -> 0}]];\n  -Pi^2 single - Pi \
pzp];\n\nDo[checkNum[\"(3.17) with [PZP] of (4.23) vs (4.24) at (a,b,k) = \" \
<> ToString[pt, InputForm],\n    \"(3.17), (4.23), (4.24)\", deltaDirect @@ \
pt, Delta24 @@ pt, 12],\n  {pt, {{13/10, 17/10, 7/10}, {4/5, 3/2, 5/2}}}];  \
(* second point: k > a, b *)\npass[]", "Input"], 
  Cell[BoxData["\"PASS 4.2.1, 4.2.3, direct integration: 0 exact, 5 numerical \
(at least 13 digits)\""], "Output"], Cell["Ledger", "Section"], 
  Cell["Grid[Prepend[ledger[[All, 1 ;; 5]],\n  {\"section\", \"check\", \
\"equation\", \"kind\", \"residual / agreement\"}],\n  Frame -> All, \
Alignment -> Left]", "Input"], 
  Cell[BoxData[TagBox[GridBox[{{"\"section\"", "\"check\"", "\"equation\"", 
        "\"kind\"", "\"residual / agreement\""}, 
       {"\"4.2.3, Landen and (4.28)\"", "\"Landen partners of r12, r34\"", 
        "\"(4.20)\"", "\"exact\"", "0"}, {"\"4.2.3, Landen and (4.28)\"", 
        "\"Landen logarithms of r12, r34\"", "\"(4.20)\"", "\"exact\"", "0"}, 
       {"\"4.2.3, Landen and (4.28)\"", 
        "\"Landen (4.19) for r12, r34 at (a,b,k) = {13/10, 17/10, 7/10}\"", 
        "\"(4.19)\"", "\"numerical\"", "\"35 digits\""}, 
       {"\"4.2.3, Landen and (4.28)\"", 
        "\"Landen (4.19) for r12, r34 at (a,b,k) = {1/2, 4/5, 3}\"", 
        "\"(4.19)\"", "\"numerical\"", "\"35 digits\""}, 
       {"\"4.2.3, Landen and (4.28)\"", "\"(4.28) vanishes at b = k\"", 
        "\"(4.28)\"", "\"exact\"", "0"}, {"\"4.2.3, Landen and (4.28)\"", 
        "\"(4.28) b-derivatives agree\"", "\"(4.28)\"", "\"exact\"", "0"}, 
       {"\"4.2.3, Landen and (4.28)\"", 
        "\"(4.28) at (a,b,k) = {13/10, 17/10, 7/10}\"", "\"(4.28)\"", 
        "\"numerical\"", "\"40 digits\""}, {"\"4.2.3, Landen and (4.28)\"", 
        "\"(4.28) at (a,b,k) = {1/2, 4/5, 3}\"", "\"(4.28)\"", 
        "\"numerical\"", "\"40 digits\""}, {"\"4.2.3, derivative\"", 
        "\"four dilogarithms remain\"", "\"(4.21)\"", "\"exact\"", "0"}, 
       {"\"4.2.3, derivative\"", "\"d/dk of (4.24) = 2 k (4.21)\"", 
        "\"(4.21), (4.24)\"", "\"exact\"", "0"}, {"\"4.2.3, large k\"", 
        "\"trilogarithm arguments tend to -1, 1/2, 1, 1\"", "\"4.2.3\"", 
        "\"exact\"", "0"}, {"\"4.2.3, large k\"", "\"P+ tends to 0\"", 
        "\"(4.25)\"", "\"exact\"", "0"}, {"\"4.2.3, large k\"", 
        "\"P- tends to 0\"", "\"(4.26)\"", "\"exact\"", "0"}, 
       {"\"4.2.3, (4.22)\"", 
        "\"(4.24) vs (4.22) at (a,b,k) = {13/10, 17/10, 7/10}\"", 
        "\"(4.22), (4.24)\"", "\"numerical\"", "\"19 digits\""}, 
       {"\"4.2.3, (4.22)\"", 
        "\"(4.24) vs (4.22) at (a,b,k) = {4/5, 3/2, 5/2}\"", 
        "\"(4.22), (4.24)\"", "\"numerical\"", "\"22 digits\""}, 
       {"\"4.2.1, 4.2.3, direct integration\"", 
        "\"loop factor vs LevinRule at (k12, k, z) = {13/10, 7/10, 1}\"", 
        "\"(4.23)\"", "\"numerical\"", "\"17 digits\""}, 
       {"\"4.2.1, 4.2.3, direct integration\"", 
        "\"loop factor vs LevinRule at (k12, k, z) = {4/5, 5/2, 6/5}\"", 
        "\"(4.23)\"", "\"numerical\"", "\"17 digits\""}, 
       {"\"4.2.1, 4.2.3, direct integration\"", "\"loop factor vs LevinRule \
at (k12, k, z) = {1, 1000001/1000000, 1}\"", "\"(4.23)\"", "\"numerical\"", 
        "\"18 digits\""}, {"\"4.2.1, 4.2.3, direct integration\"", "\"(3.17) \
with [PZP] of (4.23) vs (4.24) at (a,b,k) = {13/10, 17/10, 7/10}\"", 
        "\"(3.17), (4.23), (4.24)\"", "\"numerical\"", "\"13 digits\""}, 
       {"\"4.2.1, 4.2.3, direct integration\"", "\"(3.17) with [PZP] of \
(4.23) vs (4.24) at (a,b,k) = {4/5, 3/2, 5/2}\"", 
        "\"(3.17), (4.23), (4.24)\"", "\"numerical\"", "\"14 digits\""}}, 
      GridBoxAlignment -> {"Columns" -> {{Left}}}, AutoDelete -> False, 
      GridBoxFrame -> {"Columns" -> {{True}}, "Rows" -> {{True}}}, 
      GridBoxItemSize -> {"Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, 
        "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}}], "Grid"]], "Output"]}, 
 WindowTitle -> "chapter-04-full-difference-companion.nb", 
 StyleDefinitions -> "Default.nb", WindowSize -> {1100, 850}]
